<h4><strong>6. Manage BOM Revisions</strong></h4>
<p><p>Bill of materials is a live structure and process, so from the beginning think about how you can manage the BOM history of changes, revisions, and dates, as using wrong data can lead to delays, cost impact, and many problems.</p>
<strong>Revision Control Best Practices:</strong></p> 

<Itemize>

    <Item>Use revision letters or numbers (A, B, C... or Rev 1, Rev 2, Rev 3...)</Item>
    <Item>Document change reason and date</Item>
    <Item>Maintain revision history</Item>
    <Item>Ensure all stakeholders use current revision</Item>
    <Item>Link BOM revision to drawing revisions</Item>
    <Item>Use PDM/PLM system for automatic version control</Item>

</Itemize>
